course: dictionary
lesson: 14783
title: Prudently: careful and sensible
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Prudently is an adverb. It tells you how someone does an action: carefully, sensibly, and with thought about danger or risk. «Sam looked both ways and crossed the road prudently.» Sam did not rush or take a chance. He was careful to stay safe.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Sam crossed the road carefully and sensibly» still makes sense, so carefully and sensibly are good meanings for prudently.
explain: Prudently can also be about money. «Dad spends prudently, saving some money each month.» Here it means carefully, saving instead of wasting. Dad is not spending everything he has on things he does not need.
fact: Prudently is the adverb form of prudent, which means careful and sensible.
fact: «Prudently» means in a careful, sensible way that avoids risk.
fact: When talking about money, «prudently» means carefully, saving rather than wasting.
fact: Prudence was one of the old virtues taught in church and in lessons about how to live well.
fact: Many words ending in -ly, like prudently, tell you how someone does something.
exercise: «The climber checked the ropes prudently before she started.» What does prudently mean here? | *In a careful, sensible way that avoids risk | Happily, while singing | Quickly and without a care | Loudly and proudly
exercise: «Ella spends her pocket money prudently, saving most of it.» What does prudently mean with money? | She loses it on the way home | *Carefully, saving instead of wasting | She spends it all on sweets | She gives it away to everyone
exercise: «Ben wanted to swim in the storm, but he waited and swam prudently.» What does waited suggest? | Ben was careless | Ben was in a hurry | *Ben was thinking about the risk | Ben had forgotten the time
test: «Maya crossed the frozen pond prudently, testing the ice first.» What does testing the ice first show? | *She was being careful to avoid danger | She wanted to get wet | She was in a race | She was showing off
test: Which sentence uses prudently correctly? | *He spent his savings prudently, buying only what he needed | The sun rose prudently over the hill | He jumped off the roof prudently | She shouted prudently at the teacher
exam: «The captain steered the boat prudently around the rocks.» Which word means nearly the same as prudently here? | Recklessly | *Carefully | Lazily | Loudly
